There is a problem with the automatic timing derivation, remove ARESETN* from DDR_Interface in ROC_derived_constraints


To run, in Libero do Project/ExecutScript ROC.tcl

it will create a ROC folder in the local dir. 


MT (06/2021) 
When building from TCL with v2021:

components/fifo_mem_cntrl.tcl      must remove all of "hdl_core_delete_parameters" statements from line 35 to end
components/pattern_gen_checker     must remove all of "hdl_core_delete_parameters" statements from line 35 to end

RS485 protocol v2 (2026-09-19)
See docs/rs485-v2.md for framing, CPU compatibility, host migration and offline tests.
Run: python3 tests/rs485_v2/run_tests.py
Legacy com.py is incompatible with the v2 wire protocol. No bitstream is included.

Autonomous panel ID initialization (2026-09-23)
See docs/panel-id-reader.md for the sNVM reader, startup CPU bus handoff,
address initialization, diagnostics, and validation limitations.
Run: python3 tests/panel_id/run_tests.py
This does not yet add the FPGA-only RS485 discovery packet handler.

Manual FPGA-only golden recovery (2026-09-23)
See docs/golden-recovery.md. Activation requires an explicit user RS485 command;
CPU absence/timeouts never activate it automatically. No hardware deployment.
Run: python3 tests/golden_recovery/run_tests.py

CPU-independent ROC temperature/rail readback: docs/direct-tvs.md.
Client command: rs485_direct_read MN253 [variable ...]. Existing CPU reads remain.
